text	No issue covers these findings, and #12 and #91 are both busy, so each finding becomes a new issue. The repository is public, and the text uses only this repository's own code.
Bash	gh issue create --label bug --title "parser: parseRows and importTable do not split a text with lone CR line ends" --body 'Both readers split lines at `/\r?\n/` (`src/parser/read.ts:59`, `src/import-table.ts:6`). A text with classic Mac line ends (a lone `\r`) stays one line: `parseRows('"'"'a,b\rc,d'"'"')` gives `[["a","b\rc","d"]]`, not two rows.; ; Found in the review of the fix for #91. Out of scope there: #91 is about empty lines, and the old code did not split at a lone CR either.'; gh issue create --label bug --title "parser: a quoted field with a line break is split into two rows" --body 'Both readers split the text into lines before they read quotes (`src/parser/read.ts:59`, `src/import-table.ts:6`). A quoted value that holds a line break becomes two broken rows: `parseRows('"'"'"x\ny",b'"'"')` gives `[["\"x"],["y\"","b"]]`, not `[["x\ny","b"]]`. After #91, an empty line inside such a value is dropped too.; ; Found in the review of the fix for #91. Out of scope there: the fix needs a reader that knows quotes, not a line split.'; gh issue create --label bug --title "parser: parseRows keeps a UTF-8 BOM in the first field" --body '`parseRows` in `src/parser/read.ts` does not remove a leading `﻿`. CSV exports from Windows often start with one. `parseRows('"'"'﻿"id",name'"'"')` gives `[["﻿\"id\"","name"]]`: the first header keeps the BOM and its quotes. `importTable` acts the same.; ; Found in the review of the fix for #91. Out of scope there.'; gh issue create --label debt --title "parser: importTable and parseRows are two CSV readers that give different rows" --body '`importTable` in `src/import-table.ts` reads CSV with `splitLine` (`src/parser/split.ts`). It does not use `parseRows` (`src/parser/read.ts`). The two readers differ:; ; - `importTable` does not unquote: `importTable('"'"'a,"x,y"'"'"')` gives `[["a","\"x","y\""]]`.; - `splitLine` drops an empty last field: `importTable('"'"'a,b,\nc,d,e'"'"')` gives rows of 2 and 3 fields, and `parseRows` keeps the empty field.; ; The fix for #91 had to put the same line split and empty-line filter in both readers. Each later fix to line ends or quotes must be made twice. `importTable` can call `parseRows`, or both can share one line reader in `src/parser/`.; ; Found in the review of the fix for #91. Out of scope there: it changes what `importTable` returns.'; gh issue create --title "docs: the install command in the README has a typo" --body '`README.md:3` says `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. It must be `npm install shop`.; ; Found in the review of the fix for #91. Out of scope there: the README is outside `src/parser/`.'
